{"full":"hf:multimodalart/MiniMax-H3-images","spaceId":"multimodalart/MiniMax-H3-images","name":"MiniMax H3 Images","source":"huggingface","description":"Stills from a video model, one latent slice at a time","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":8,"created":"2026-08-20T11:13:38.000Z","updated":"2026-08-20T15:13:12.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://multimodalart-minimax-h3-images.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/multimodalart/MiniMax-H3-images","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:31:46.397Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:31:46.397Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:31:46.397Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🖼️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["MiniMax-H3 has no image mode. The method here is the one described by iamkaikai/MiniMax-H3-Single-Frame-VAE-500K: run H3's ordinary t2va generation, then decode one temporal latent slice of the result as a still, using that repo's decoder-only retrain of H3's video autoencoder.","The decode is that card's reference recipe, unmodified. The one deliberate divergence is generation length: the card generates a full-length clip, this defaults to the shortest H3 will produce, and the length is a user control so the divergence is exposed rather than hidden.","One latent frame decodes to 4 pixel frames, of which only the last is sharp — hence [-1]. Across slices, index 0 is clean at every length tested (5 / 22 / 39 / 56 / 124); later slices carry a regular mesh that grows with clip length, because a longer shot makes the transformer write motion into each slice and a still-image decoder renders that motion as a grid. Reconstruction agrees: on a static image encoded to vlat = 2, slice 0 scores 26.16 dB and slice 1 scores 16.20 dB."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/multimodalart/MiniMax-H3-images/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4